/-!
# The linear-three-over-four completion argument

The native projective flag amalgam has a core-free whole Borel in every
faithful completion. An equivariant comparison of its typed coset graph
with the native graph gives an isomorphism preserving both endpoint ranges.

For every finite completion, two endpoint involutions outside the whole Borel
whose product has order three supply the geometric smallness premises.
Recognition of the resulting order-four plane completes the finite PSL₃(4)
specialization of Aschbacher–Smith F.4.26 (printed p.288), preserving both
parabolic ranges without any additional geometric or recognition hypothesis.
-/
